<div class="container">
    <span style="font-size:18px;font-family:'Global Monospace';">
        Uttarakhand tourism promotes the state's "Devbhoomi" (Land of the Gods) image, which includes nature, adventure,
        and spirituality.<span style="font-size:18px;font-family:'Global Monospace';">
            The Uttarakhand Tourism Development Board is the governing body that aims to make the
            state a leading global destination by developing its tourism resources sustainably and responsibly.
        </span>
        The state is known for its Himalayan peaks, diverse ecosystems, abundant wildlife, religious pilgrimage sites,
        and adventure activities like trekking and river rafting.
    </span>
    <br />

    <h1 class="text text-success" style="text-decoration:underline">Overview</h1>
    <br />
    <img src="~/content/images/image4.jpeg" alt="image4" height="350px" width="400px" style="float:right;margin-left:15px "  />
  
    <h4 class="text text-primary">Region: </h4><p> A state in northern India, located in the Himalayas.</p>
    <h4 class="text text-primary">Known as:</h4> "Devbhoomi" (Land of the Gods) due to its numerous Hindu temples and pilgrimage sites.
    <h4 class="text text-primary">Key offerings:</h4> A combination of natural beauty, adventure activities, and spiritual journeys.
    <br />
    <h1 class="text text-primary" style="text-decoration:dotted"> About UTDB</h1><br />
    <span>
        Uttarakhand Tourism Development Board is the highest body to advise the Government on all matters relating to tourism in the State. The statutory board is chaired by the Tourism Minister Govt. of Uttarakhand and Chief Secretary of Uttarakhand is its vice chairman. The Principal Secretary/ Secretary tourism acts as Chief Executive Officer. It also has five non-official members from the private sector and experts in tourism related matters.

        The board also functions as a regulatory and licensing Authority.
    </span>

    <h5>Mission   Vision</h5>

    <span>
        To place Uttarakhand on the tourism map of the world as one of the leading tourist destinations, and to make Uttarakhand synonymous with tourism.

        To develop the manifold tourism related resources of the State in an eco-friendly manner, with the active participation of the private sector and the local host communities.

        To develop tourism as a major source of employment and income/revenue generation and as a pivot of the economic and social development in the State.
    </span>

    <h5>About Us</h5>
    <span>
        As tourism continues to thrive in the state, Uttarakhand has become a year-round destination for nature lovers, pilgrims, adventure seekers, and culture enthusiasts.

        Join us in exploring the wonders of Uttarakhand — where development meets preservation, and growth leads to deeper experiences.
</span>
